{"id": "EUVD-2026-82088", "enisaUuid": "a3fa8f8b-b46f-3e2b-97ca-1e860411b715", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/tegra241-cmdqv: Don't fall back to a freed smmu after devm_krealloc()\n\n__tegra241_cmdqv_probe() uses devm_krealloc() to grow @smmu into the larger\ntegra241_cmdqv, which frees the original @smmu once it relocates. A failure\nafter that returned NULL, and the caller then dereferenced the freed @smmu\non its fallback path.\n\nReturn an int and take @smmu by reference instead, then update *smmu to the\nreallocated pointer after devm_krealloc() succeeds, so the caller and its\nfallback path both use the live @smmu rather than the freed original.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:38", "baseScore": 7.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea2edb27ef2648d8687cd0fc3ec3ba1793436e7e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/268cbe3a36ae57a2ec09601f343b92f6f092d505", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86197679b293f0601c3331d545f99a70a7780aa9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d4d05f55e9da646ec03adfa77260eb46f4163749"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90427", "GHSA-7wgr-jrpm-fgrv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d145ab1-a600-3202-af39-13b862aaa984", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "141de942-dadf-3233-b4f7-da13d739eefa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1ca0e35a-a1ce-3bd3-aa3c-98e51224f0de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "51700fa4-9b26-3870-b1aa-82b0094d6870", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "918eb5c856f6ce4cf93b4b38e4b5e156905c5943 <ea2edb27ef2648d8687cd0fc3ec3ba1793436e7e"}, {"id": "51777ebc-eac4-3c0d-a538-e752aca210c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "552b943f-f13f-30ff-9340-b27bdf9f9f51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "918eb5c856f6ce4cf93b4b38e4b5e156905c5943 <d4d05f55e9da646ec03adfa77260eb46f4163749"}, {"id": "64909f5c-3f74-3a69-932e-b8d287cad6f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "918eb5c856f6ce4cf93b4b38e4b5e156905c5943 <86197679b293f0601c3331d545f99a70a7780aa9"}, {"id": "83158ca9-7a0c-3d6d-af4c-efdfd7a211ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "bd3080dd-cb94-3695-afc4-9c13557f7176", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "918eb5c856f6ce4cf93b4b38e4b5e156905c5943 <268cbe3a36ae57a2ec09601f343b92f6f092d505"}, {"id": "fdb9975a-b48f-315f-8b12-7f86277f593b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9b5c786a-f141-30a9-bebd-cfe4b39b4abd", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}